    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57bb123b_587f6c02",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-20T21:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t need both nvmem_buffer_tab[] and nvmem_get_users().  We can just say this:\n\n  extern uin32_t nvmem_user_sizes[NVMEM_NUM_USERS];\n\nand require that those terms be defined somewhere else. We can sanity-check that table in nvmem_init().\n\nYou might add a comment noting that the total of the all the user_sizes can be no more than \n\n  (CONFIG_FLASH_NVMEM_SIZE / 2) - sizeof(struct nvmem_tag)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 50,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c84cfcd_283f4fc5",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-23T21:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I changed the array nvmem_buffer_tab to nvmem_user_sizes[] as that\u0027s a better description and am now making the array available to common/nvmem.c via an extern declaration. nvmem_init() builds a starting offset array using the sizes.",
      "parentUuid": "57bb123b_587f6c02",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 50,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
