      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57bb123b_dbdd1623",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 277,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-20T21:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I really don\u0027t like all these signed values. They lead to rollover and/or awkward casts, especially when dealing with 32-bit addresses that may legitimately have the high bit set. Make everything uint32_t. A value of 0xffffffff makes no sense for base, addr, or offset, so we can use that value for invalid/undefined if we need to.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 277,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c84cfcd_25af78a3",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 277,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-23T21:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I changed the offsets to unsigned. What I was trying to achieve was to make the error checking in terms of lengths easier. When the offset is unsigned then you had pointed out that checking \u0027offset + len \u003c\u003d user_size\u0027 may not be sufficient due to the possibility off a wrap.",
      "parentUuid": "57bb123b_dbdd1623",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 276,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 277,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "57bb123b_db0516b6",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 289,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-20T21:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could create an array of constants for this purpose in nvmem_init(), so we don\u0027t have to sum up the lengths every time.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 287,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 289,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c84cfcd_e57f5000",
        "filename": "common/nvmem.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 289,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-23T21:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I made the change as you suggested. Creating a nvmem_user_start_offset[NVMEM_NUM_USERS] array so it\u0027s only computed once. The array is populated when nvmem_init() is called.",
      "parentUuid": "57bb123b_db0516b6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 287,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 289,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "78126d2a772bf195e21b065f568444670c179267",
